# Line-ending policy.
#
# The repository is consumed on Linux/WSL (primary target) and authored on
# Windows. Without this file a Windows checkout would give shell scripts CRLF
# endings, and bash would fail with "\r: command not found" on every line.
#
# Only the paths listed here are normalised; the Keil firmware tree is
# deliberately left alone so its existing line endings are not churned.

# Shell scripts and debugger command files must be LF, always.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.gdb   text eol=lf

# Source and documentation: normalise to LF in the repository.
# NOTE: firmware C sources are intentionally NOT listed. The Keil project tree
# keeps whatever endings it already has, so adding this file does not churn
# files that are never built or tested on Linux.
*.py     text eol=lf
*.cpp    text eol=lf
*.hpp    text eol=lf
*.cmake  text eol=lf
CMakeLists.txt text eol=lf

# Configuration and docs.
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf

# Binary assets that must never be touched.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.zip    binary
*.hex    binary
*.bin    binary
*.axf    binary
